AMediaCodec_getOutputBuffer() already points at the buffer's range offset; FFmpeg
added BufferInfo.offset again on the NDK path, cutting 12 bytes from every frame of
OMX.qcom.video.encoder.vp8 (Snapdragon 855). Upstream: to be sent to ffmpeg-devel.

--- a/libavcodec/mediacodec_wrapper.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodec_wrapper.c
@@ -2270,7 +2270,11 @@
     ssize_t ret;
 
     ret = AMediaCodec_dequeueOutputBuffer(codec->impl, &buf_info, timeoutUs);
-    info->offset = buf_info.offset;
+    /* AMediaCodec_getOutputBuffer() returns ABuffer::data(), which already
+     * points at the range offset, unlike the JNI ByteBuffer address. Callers
+     * add info->offset to that pointer, so report 0 here, or bytes are lost
+     * (OMX.qcom.video.encoder.vp8 uses offset 12). */
+    info->offset = 0;
     info->size = buf_info.size;
     info->presentationTimeUs = buf_info.presentationTimeUs;
     info->flags = buf_info.flags;
